title Cassette Bluetooth (T4, synthetic names): the Input picker: a USB card (plain row), a connected headset (Evolve 65, 16 kHz, Bluetooth headset, speech quality), a headset whose microphone is off and the chosen headset that is not connected (both dimmed, the reason under the name; the long name wraps and its row grows); the footer; Enter on a dimmed row says why and stays; Input level greyed (Not applicable)
sizes 320x480 480x320 480x800 640x480 800x480 480x480 720x720
ppmm 608
env CASSETTE_DEMO idle
env CASSETTE_DEMO_BT input
env CASSETTE_LAYOUT_CHECK 1

wait 500
key s
wait 300
expect text "Input level"
expect text "Not applicable"
shot settings
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key enter
wait 300
expect text "USB Audio Device"
expect text "Evolve 65"
expect text "16 kHz"
expect text "Bluetooth headsets record speech quality (16 kHz)"
shot input-picker
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key up
key enter
wait 300
expect text "Not available: The headset microphone is off"
say Enter on the headset with its microphone off: the notice says why, the picker stays
shot input-picker-mic-off
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key down
key enter
wait 300
expect text "Not available: Not connected"
shot input-picker-not-connected
expect notext "LAYOUT FAIL"
key esc
wait 300
key esc
wait 300
expect text "SOFT"
expect text "BT"
expect noquit
